cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TinyAudit, please cite it as below."
title: "TinyAudit: auditing small models for fairness, explainability, and uncertainty within a microcontroller-class footprint"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Doke
    given-names: Atharva
  - family-names: Tumuluri
    given-names: Kasyap
repository-code: "https://github.com/tinyaudit/tinyaudit"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-01-01"
keywords:
  - fairness
  - explainability
  - uncertainty quantification
  - tinyml
  - model compression
  - responsible ai
abstract: >-
  TinyAudit is an auditing pipeline that jointly measures point-prediction
  fairness, group-conditional predictive uncertainty, and feature-level
  explainability under a fixed memory and FLOPs budget consistent with
  microcontroller-class deployment. It is benchmarked on UCI Adult,
  Folktables (ACSIncome), and COMPAS, and characterizes how int8
  quantization and magnitude pruning shift each audited metric.
